  "id": "COMPOUND:20768 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Gamma-Fagarine is implicated in the interaction with Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of molecular targets, all of which are ultimately directed toward Raji cells. The evidence suggests that Gamma-Fagarine acts as a target for multiple compounds, including (5S)-5-[(2S)-1,2-dihydroxypropan-2-yl]-2-methylcyclohex-2-en-1-one, 23-Epivepaol, and Ginsenoside Rs5, which in turn target Phosphodiesterase 6C. This indicates a potential pathway where Gamma-Fagarine may interact with these compounds, which then exert their effects on Phosphodiesterase 6C. The shared target of these compounds with Phosphodiesterase 6C suggests a possible mechanism of action involving the modulation of this enzyme, possibly through competitive or non-competitive inhibition. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Phosphodiesterase 6C as a downstream effector in the signaling cascade initiated by Gamma-Fagarine and its related compounds.",
